      "learned": "Discount is the actual shilling reduction on the marked price: Discount = Marked Price − Sale Price. Percentage Discount expresses that reduction as a proportion of the marked price: Percentage Discount = (Discount ÷ Marked Price) × 100. Both formulas are reversible — given a percentage discount, students can recover the sale price or the marked price. Learners also recognised that a larger percentage discount is not always a larger shilling saving if the marked prices differ.",
